---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pagination:
  data: emst.variants
  size: 1
  alias: v
permalink: "{{ v.url }}"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "How this role is changing: {{ v.role.title }} ({{ v.actorLabel }})"
---
{% import "macros.njk" as m %}
<h1>{{ v.role.title }} <span class="emst-muted">· {{ v.actorLabel }}</span></h1>
<p>Authority position: {{ v.authorityPositionLabel or "not set" }}{% if v.subtypeLabel %} · {{ v.subtypeLabel }}{% endif %}{% if v.industry %} · industry: {{ v.industry | replace("-", " ") }}{% endif %} <span class="emst-muted">(editorial classification)</span>. Other variants:
{% for o in v.role.variants %}{% if o.id != v.id %}<a href="{{ o.url | url }}">{{ o.actorLabel }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}{% else %}none{% endfor %}.</p>
<nav aria-label="Views for this role variant"><p><strong>How it is changing</strong> · <a href="{{ v.gapUrl | url }}">Gap check</a> · <a href="{{ v.pathwaysUrl | url }}">Where it can lead</a></p></nav>

<h2>In short</h2>
<p class="emst-lede">{{ v.definition or v.role.functionStatement }}</p>
{{ m.meta(v.tier, v.evidence, "agent draft · lifecycle: " + (v.lifecycleState or "not set")) }}
{% if v.actor == "federal" or v.actor == "state" %}{{ m.hrDisclaimer() }}{% endif %}

<h2>How the work is shifting</h2>
<figure class="emst-figure" data-figure data-use-tier="{{ v.tier.tier }}" data-evidence="{{ v.evidence.label }}">
  <figcaption>No task in this role has a v2 multi-rater change assessment yet</figcaption>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 640 {{ 20 + v.levelCounts.length * 34 }}" role="img" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" width="640" height="{{ 20 + v.levelCounts.length * 34 }}">
    <defs><pattern id="pend-{{ v.slug }}" width="8" height="8" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><rect width="8" height="8" fill="#ffffff"/><circle cx="4" cy="4" r="1.6" fill="#565c65"/></pattern></defs>
    {% set maxN = v.bundle.length %}
    {% for l in v.levelCounts %}
    {% set y = 6 + loop.index0 * 34 %}{% set wA = l.assessed | barWidth(maxN, 470) %}{% set wP = l.pending | barWidth(maxN, 470) %}
    <text x="0" y="{{ y + 17 }}" font-size="13" fill="#1b1b1b">{{ l.key | titlecase }}</text>
    {% if wA > 0 %}<rect x="80" y="{{ y }}" width="{{ wA }}" height="24" fill="#1a4480" stroke="#1b1b1b"/>{% endif %}
    <rect x="{{ 80 + wA }}" y="{{ y }}" width="{{ wP }}" height="24" fill="url(#pend-{{ v.slug }})" stroke="#1b1b1b"/>
    <text x="{{ 88 + wA + wP }}" y="{{ y + 17 }}" font-size="13" fill="#1b1b1b">{{ l.assessed }} of {{ l.total }} assessed</text>
    {% endfor %}
  </svg>
  <p>Tasks at each role level by assessment status. Dotted means assessment pending. Counts, not time shares: time shares are job-analysis values and stay hidden until a job analysis confirms them.</p>
  <div class="emst-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Tasks by assessment status and role level">
  <table class="usa-table usa-table--compact">
    <caption>Tasks by assessment status and role level (table of the chart)</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Role level</th><th scope="col">Proficiency band</th><th scope="col" class="emst-num">Tasks</th><th scope="col" class="emst-num">Assessed (v2 multi-rater)</th><th scope="col" class="emst-num">Assessment pending</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{% for l in v.levelCounts %}<tr><td>{{ l.key | titlecase }}</td><td>{% for b in l.band | uniq %}{{ b }} ({{ emst.labels.level[b] | lower }}){% if not loop.last %} to {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td><td class="emst-num">{{ l.total }}</td><td class="emst-num">{{ l.assessed }}</td><td class="emst-num">{{ l.pending }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p><strong>Evidence mix:</strong> v1 single-analyst codes exist for some tasks. They appear only in each task's evidence drawer and are not counted here.</p>
  <p><strong>External context:</strong> not in this build. Occupation-level external exposure indices are third-party licensed and excluded from release files; task-level external values need a human-reviewed O*NET task crosswalk first. Values are never averaged across indices.</p>
  <p class="emst-muted">Computed with rule role-change@0.1.0 (interim; reference implementation in the explorer build).</p>
  {{ m.meta(v.tier, v.evidence, "computed at build from release records") }}
</figure>

<h2>Tasks in this role</h2>
<p>Which tasks the role bundles, at which levels, and which are formation tasks are <em>editorial draft</em> design values (agent-drafted, unreviewed). Importance, time share and the critical and needed-at-entry flags are job-analysis values: they read "Assessment pending (job analysis)" until a named person reviews them.</p>
<div class="emst-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Task bundle">
<table class="usa-table usa-table--compact usa-table--striped" data-figure data-use-tier="{{ v.tier.tier }}" data-evidence="{{ v.evidence.label }}">
  <caption>Task bundle for this variant ({{ v.bundle.length }} tasks; editorial draft). {{ m.tierBadge(v.tier) }} {{ m.evBadge(v.evidence) }}</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Task</th><th scope="col">Role levels</th><th scope="col">Formation task</th><th scope="col">Importance, time share, critical, needed at entry</th><th scope="col">How it is changing</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for b in v.bundle %}
  <tr><td><a href="#{{ b.task.anchor }}">{{ b.task.statement }}</a></td><td>{{ b.roleLevels | join(", ") or "all" }}</td><td>{{ "yes" if b.formationTask else "no" }}</td>
  <td>{% if b.ja.renders %}importance {{ b.importance }}; {{ b.timeShare | pct }} of time; critical {{ "yes" if b.critical else "no" }}; needed at entry {{ "yes" if b.neededAtEntry else "no" }} ({{ b.ja.status }}){% else %}<span class="emst-pending">{{ b.ja.text }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
  <td>{% if b.task.exposure.renders %}{{ m.gateText(b.task.exposure) }}{% else %}<span class="emst-pending">Assessment pending</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% for b in v.bundle %}{{ m.taskBlock(b.task, emst.gateLabels, "levels: " + (b.roleLevels | join(", ") or "all")) }}{% endfor %}

<h2>Drivers: policy instruments and signals</h2>
{% set il = v.instrumentLinks %}
{% if il.typed.length or il.viaMech.length %}
<div class="emst-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Policy instruments for this variant">
<table class="usa-table usa-table--compact" data-figure data-use-tier="describe" data-evidence="E">
  <caption>Policy instruments that shape this work, with status as of {{ emst.release.date }}. <span class="emst-badge emst-badge--tier" data-badge="tier"><span class="emst-badge__k">Use tier:</span>describe</span> <span class="emst-badge emst-badge--ev" data-badge="evidence"><span class="emst-badge__k">Evidence:</span>dated events from cited sources; the links to this role are agent drafts, unreviewed</span></caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Instrument</th><th scope="col">How it is linked</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Dated events</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for x in il.typed %}<tr><td>{{ x.i.title }}</td><td>{{ x.via }}</td><td>{{ m.instrumentState(x.i) }}</td><td>{{ m.instrumentEvents(x.i) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  {% for x in il.viaMech %}<tr><td>{{ x.i.title }}</td><td>{{ x.via }}</td><td>{{ m.instrumentState(x.i) }}</td><td>{{ m.instrumentEvents(x.i) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% if il.viaMechTotal > il.viaMech.length %}<p class="emst-muted">{{ il.viaMechTotal - il.viaMech.length }} more instruments reach this role through the same mechanisms; see <a href="{{ '/whats-coming/' | url }}">What's coming</a>.</p>{% endif %}
{% else %}<p>No policy instrument is linked to this variant in this build.</p>{% endif %}
{% set c = v.change %}
{% if c.drivers.length %}
<p>Signals recorded about this role or its primary work function ({{ v.role.primaryWorkFunctionLabel }}). All are <strong>watch</strong> signals: none yet meets the evidence rule for a change indicator (two independent signal families, human-reviewed).</p>
<ul class="emst-cards">{% for s in c.drivers %}{{ m.signalItem(s) }}{% endfor %}</ul>
{% else %}
<p>No change signal in this build targets this role or its primary work function. "No signal yet" is a finding, not a reassurance.</p>
{% endif %}
{% if c.actorWide %}<p class="emst-muted">{{ c.actorWide }} further signal{{ "s" if c.actorWide != 1 }} describe{{ "s" if c.actorWide == 1 }} {{ v.actorLabel | lower if v.actor == "federal" or v.actor == "state" else "this kind of" }} employers as a whole (for example agency headcounts), not this role, so {{ "they are" if c.actorWide != 1 else "it is" }} listed only in <a href="{{ '/whats-coming/' | url }}">What's coming</a>.</p>{% endif %}
{% if c.withheld %}<p class="emst-muted">{{ c.withheld }} signal{{ "s" if c.withheld != 1 }} withheld: {{ "they rest" if c.withheld != 1 else "it rests" }} on a claim the verification pass has not re-checked.</p>{% endif %}

<h2>Forming in this role (watch, emerging or proposed)</h2>
{% if c.emerging.length %}
<ul class="usa-list">{% for e in c.emerging %}<li><a href="{{ e.url | url }}">{{ e.title }}</a> {{ m.lifecycleTag(e.lifecycleState) }}{% if e.reviewBy %} review by {{ e.reviewBy }}{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% else %}<p>No competency this role targets is marked emerging or proposed.</p>{% endif %}
{% if v.emergingNext.length %}<p>Emerging roles named as next steps: {% for r in v.emergingNext %}<a href="{{ r.url | url }}">{{ r.title }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} (see What's coming).</p>{% endif %}

<h2>What stays human</h2>
<p><span class="emst-pending">{{ emst.gateLabels.assessment_pending }}</span> A descriptive "stays human" rationale is shown only when it comes from a v2 assessment that passes the display gate.</p>
{% if c.formation.length %}<p>{{ c.formation.length }} tasks in this variant are flagged as formation tasks, the work through which judgment is learned (editorial draft).</p>{% endif %}

<h2>Competencies this role targets</h2>
<div class="emst-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Competency targets">
<table class="usa-table usa-table--compact" data-figure data-use-tier="{{ v.role.tier.tier }}" data-evidence="{{ v.role.evidence.label }}">
  <caption>Target levels by role level: design statements drafted by AI agents, not findings. Not yet reviewed by practitioners. {{ m.tierBadge(v.role.tier) }} {{ m.evBadge(v.role.evidence) }}</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Competency</th>{% for l in v.role.roleLevels %}<th scope="col">{{ l.key | titlecase }}</th>{% endfor %}{% if v.actor == "federal" %}<th scope="col">Federal applicability (computed)</th>{% endif %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for t in v.role.competencyTargets %}
  <tr><td><a href="{{ t.competency.url | url }}">{{ t.competency.title }}</a> {{ m.moduleTag(t.competency) }} {{ m.lifecycleTag(t.competency.lifecycleState) if t.competency.lifecycleState != "established" }}</td>
  {% for l in v.role.roleLevels %}<td>{{ t.targetLevels[l.key] or "–" }}</td>{% endfor %}
  {% if v.actor == "federal" %}<td>{% if t.competency.federal %}{% if t.competency.federal.value == "basis-not-yet-linked" %}basis not yet linked{% elif t.competency.federal.value == "not-shown-unverified" %}not shown (unverified instrument){% elif t.competency.federal.basisWithheld %}indeterminate (a linked instrument is withheld from this release){% else %}{{ t.competency.federal.value | replace("-", " ") }}{% if not t.competency.federal.basisLinked %}, basis not yet linked{% elif not t.competency.federal.basisVerified %}, basis status not yet verified{% endif %}{% endif %}{% else %}not computed (no federal enactment linked){% endif %}</td>{% endif %}</tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="emst-muted">Importance and "distinguishing" flags for these competencies are job-analysis values: assessment pending (job analysis).{% if v.actor == "federal" %} Federal applicability is read only from the computed view ({{ "prototype computation; 'required basis' is never shown from it" if emst.venue.source == "wp05-prototype" else ("rule " + emst.venue.rule + " over the release records") }}; as of {{ emst.venue.asOf }}). Nothing is excluded from this view (the EMST project lead's default).{% endif %}</p>

<h2>Crosswalks and credentials</h2>
{% if v.credentialGates.length %}<p>Credentials that may be involved (agent-drafted link, not a requirement; the credential's issuer was checked against a cited source): {% for g in v.credentialGates %}{{ g.title }} (drafted as {{ g.kind }}){% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>{% endif %}
{% if v.credentialGatesPending %}<p class="emst-muted">{{ v.credentialGatesPending }} credential gate{{ "s" if v.credentialGatesPending != 1 }} not shown until the issuer is verified.</p>{% endif %}
{% if v.grade %}<p>Indicative {{ v.grade.scheme + " " if v.grade.scheme }}grade band{{ "s" if v.grade.bands.length != 1 }}: {% for b in v.grade.bands %}{% if b.level %}{{ b.level | titlecase }} {% endif %}{{ b.band }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %} <span class="emst-muted">({{ v.grade.label + "; " if v.grade.label }}judgment by EMST's federal HR agent, an AI agent; not reviewed by a classifier)</span>.</p>{% endif %}
{{ m.crosswalkTable(v.crosswalks, "Draft crosswalks for this variant", true) }}
{% if not v.crosswalks.length %}<p>No variant-level crosswalk rows in this build.</p>{% endif %}

<h2>Next steps</h2>
<ul class="usa-list">
  <li><a href="{{ v.gapUrl | url }}">Check development gaps for this role</a> (runs only in your browser)</li>
  <li><a href="{{ v.pathwaysUrl | url }}">See where this role can lead</a> (exploratory)</li>
  <li>Print this page for a role-change brief. Every printed claim carries its use tier and evidence label.</li>
</ul>
